{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122497","id":4295405352,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAAavKA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122497","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122497.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122497.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122497","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122497/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122497/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122497/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/577a4bb8ca3656f0537d2bdca2b0a4d8f4163dc2","number":122497,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"macOS: Fix embedded process responsiveness","user":{"login":"SamiJ","id":990828,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5MDgyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/990828?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamiJ","html_url":"https://github.com/SamiJ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamiJ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamiJ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamiJ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamiJ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamiJ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamiJ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamiJ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamiJ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamiJ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #122489\r\n\r\nOn macOS, embedded game processes are registered with LaunchServices but use a custom loop that never enters the `NSApplication` run loop. The process therefore never signals that it has finished launching, which causes Activity Monitor to report it as \"Not Responding\" even though the embedded game remains interactive.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis changes `OS_MacOS_Embedded` to use the `NSApplication` event loop, with Godot's frame iteration driven by a `kCFRunLoopBeforeWaiting` observer in the same way as the regular macOS loop.\r\n\r\nWhen the game exits, the observer is removed, `NSApp` is stopped, and an application-defined event is posted so the run loop returns even when the embedded process has no window-generated events. Run-loop wakeups also respect `wait_timer` so event-aware frame pacing can sleep correctly.\r\n\r\nValidation:\r\n\r\n- Built the macOS ARM64 development editor and `.app` bundle.\r\n- Reproduced the issue with the Compatibility renderer and confirmed the embedded process no longer appears as \"Not Responding\" in Activity Monitor.\r\n- Confirmed `LSApplicationHasSignalledItIsReady=true`.\r\n- Verified graceful self-quit through both raw and bundled launch paths.\r\n- Exercised the event-aware frame-delay path.\r\n- Ran `git diff --check`.\r\n\r\n## AI disclosure\r\n\r\nOpenAI Codex assisted with investigating the issue and drafting the implementation. Claude Code and GPT-5.6 Sol were used for independent code review. I built and manually verified the resulting fix in Activity Monitor.","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-17T10:25:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T09:05:15Z","closed_at":"2026-08-17T10:26:58Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1a9cdf4e758768ea84cdd0a299770894df402394","assignee":null,"assignees